-- Q187 [score:6] short-stem(10w) -> expand stem with scenario, cite ASC 350
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = 'Thornfield Industries acquired Barrington Electronics in a business combination and recognized $3.8 million of goodwill. Two years after the acquisition, Thornfield''s CFO must determine the level at which goodwill impairment testing should be performed. Under ASC 350, goodwill acquired in a business combination is tested for impairment at:',
  explanation = 'Under ASC 350-20-35, goodwill is tested for impairment at the reporting unit level. A reporting unit is defined as an operating segment or one level below an operating segment (a component). Goodwill is allocated to reporting units that benefit from the synergies of the business combination, and impairment testing occurs annually at that level. Choice A is incorrect because goodwill is not tested at the individual asset level — it is an asset that relates to a group of assets within a reporting unit. Choice D is incorrect because testing at the consolidated entity level would aggregate reporting units with different economic characteristics, potentially masking impairment in one unit with strong performance in another.'
