-- Q478 [score:6] length-cuing -> balance choice lengths
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = '["Recorded entirely as goodwill on the investor''s books and never subsequently amortized or adjusted","Ignored because the equity method does not track or adjust for basis differences over time","Expensed immediately as acquisition costs in the period the investment is initially acquired","Allocated to identifiable assets based on fair value differences, with any remainder as goodwill"]',
  explanation = 'When an equity method investor pays more than its share of book value, the excess is analyzed similarly to a purchase price allocation under ASC 323-10-35. The excess is allocated to specific identifiable assets (such as undervalued inventory, PP&E, or intangibles) and amortized as those items are consumed or depreciated. Any remaining excess is treated as equity method goodwill, which is not amortized but is tested for impairment as part of the overall investment balance. Choice A is incorrect because recording the entire excess as goodwill ignores identifiable fair value differences in specific assets and liabilities that should be separately allocated and amortized. Choice C is incorrect because the excess represents a basis difference in net assets, not an acquisition cost — it is systematically recognized as the underlying assets are consumed.'
