-- Q465 [score:6] short-stem(10w) -> expand stem with scenario, cite GASB 34
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = 'The finance director of the City of Clearwater is preparing the government-wide statement of activities for the fiscal year ended June 30, 2026. She must decide how to categorize the city''s $85 million in expenses across police, fire, parks, public works, and administration. Under GASB Statement No. 34, expenses in the government-wide statement of activities are reported by:',
  explanation = 'Under GASB Statement No. 34 (paragraph 38), the statement of activities presents expenses by function or program — such as general government, public safety, education, highways, and health and welfare. Program revenues (charges for services, operating grants, and capital grants) are reported directly alongside the function they support, and the net expense or revenue for each function is displayed. This functional format helps users assess the net cost of each government service. Choice A is incorrect because object classification (salaries, supplies, utilities) is used in detailed budgetary schedules and fund-level reporting, not in the government-wide statement of activities. Choice C is incorrect because fund-based presentation is used in governmental fund financial statements — the government-wide statements consolidate all governmental activities into a single column regardless of fund structure.'
